senses.gloss:
वीरण, अस्, m., N. of a sage (father of Vīraṇī);
of the father of Asiknī; of a teacher of the Yajur-
veda; (ई), f. a side-glance, leer; a deep place; N.
of a daughter of Vīraṇa and mother of Cākṣuṣa;
(अम्), n. a fragrant grass, Andropogon Muricatus;
[cf. विरण, वैरिण.]

वि-रुग्ण, अस्, आ, अम् (less correctly written वि-
रुग्न), broken to pieces, torn asunder; bent;
blunted; destroyed.
